[statement]
A package installed does not rule out a candidate whose dependency on its
name no package could ever meet: `python3` 3.14, installed for `a`, does
not rule out `py` r10, which needs `python3~3.12`, and no `python3` 3.12 is
offered; apk chooses `py` r10 and refuses, rather than install r9. Contrast
`a-holder-rules-out-a-dependent-another-version-would-meet`.

[repository]
P:python3
V:3.14.10-r1

P:a
V:1
D:python3~3.14

P:py
V:1.1-r9

P:py
V:1.1-r10
D:python3~3.12

[request]
a
py

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   python3-3.14.10-r1:
|     breaks: py-1.1-r10[python3~3.12]
|     satisfies: a-1[python3~3.14]
refused
